{
  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "The dominant finding from 5 completed experiments is that scvi_n200 as RNA encoder produces a massive accuracy jump (config_045: 0.706) over scgpt (~0.47–0.54), making it the clear best encoder. Config_045 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the current best. The key remaining uncertainty is whether transformer aggregation can further improve upon avgpool when paired with scvi_n200's rich latent representations—scvi_n200 encodes profiles into a learned latent space where attention-based aggregation may capture cross-profile interactions that simple averaging misses. Config_024 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is the most direct exploitation of the best configuration, testing the one architectural axis (aggregation) where evidence from scgpt experiments (avgpool slightly > transformer) may not transfer to the fundamentally different scvi_n200 latent space. This is the highest-value single experiment: if transformer helps, we get a new best; if not, we confirm avgpool is optimal and can focus remaining budget on other axes. Expected cost: ~5–6 GPU hours (transformer aggregation adds overhead over avgpool's 4.82 h baseline, but imagenet_vit_l and scvi_n200 are the same as config_045), which is moderate and justified by the potential accuracy gain."
}

